  "id": "drug-withdrawal",
  "term": "drug withdrawal",
  "definition": "Drug withdrawal is a substance-specific brain and body syndrome that can occur when use of an addictive drug is stopped or reduced. It can involve a range of physical and psychological symptoms, often distressing or painful, such as craving, anxiety, low mood, sleep problems, nausea, sweating, body aches, tremors, hallucinations, or convulsions.",
